INT. HOSPITAL - STAFF LOUNGE - 3 AM

Vending machine hum. A couch with a stain no one will claim. A TV on mute plays a late-night infomercial.

DR. ANIKA SHARMA (30s, scrubs, hair undone) sprawls on the couch. NURSE BARTHOLOMEW "BART" KINSELLA (50s, glasses on a chain) stirs instant coffee. RESIDENT DR. TOMASZ NOWAK (20s, wired) flips through a chart. TECH LUCINDA FAIRCHILD (20s, headphones) eats crackers. ORDERLY MARCUS OYELOWO (40s, mop in hand) leans in the doorway. And attending DR. REGINALD PEMBERTON (60s, bow tie, exhausted dignity) sits very still in the armchair.

BART
(to the room)
Anyone want donuts? They're from Tuesday.

LUCINDA
Pass.

TOMASZ
Is Tuesday old?

ANIKA
Tuesday is archaeological.

PEMBERTON
(to himself)
Three hours until rounds.

A monitor beeps down the hall. All six stiffen. Anika sits up. Tomasz drops the chart. Bart sets down the coffee. Lucinda pulls off one earphone. Marcus straightens. Pemberton opens one eye.

The beep resolves into a steady rhythm. Nobody moves.

PEMBERTON (CONT'D)
False alarm.

They exhale together. Anika slumps back. Tomasz picks up the chart. Bart returns to stirring.

MARCUS
(to no one)
I hate nights.

LUCINDA
Everyone hates nights.

PEMBERTON
(gently)
Nights are where we find out who we are.

BART
(muttering)
Tired, apparently.
